//! The `border-image-width` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property sets
//! the width of an element's [border
//! image](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/border-image).
//!
//! Initial: 1. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: refer to the width or height of the border image area.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - auto: The width of the border is made equal to the intrinsic width or height (whichever is
//! applicable) of the corresponding `border-image-slice`. If the image does not have the required
//! intrinsic dimension, the corresponding `border-width` is used instead.
//!
//! Grammar: [ <length-percentage [0,∞]> | <number [0,∞]> | auto ]{1,4}
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-borders-4/#propdef-border-image-width
//!
//! Author guide:
